{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794042751,"nonce":"GM+24/WThZOJjD2AFCFjzS6fmy0=","title":"iOS: the soft keyboard drops while typing in text input, textarea and code editor","message":"On iOS browsers the keyboard does not stay up in the web host's text input, textarea and the code editor.\n\nThe host sets the hidden editor's inputMode to none whenever a state report says nothing is editable. iOS dismisses a raised keyboard on that change and does not raise it again outside a user gesture.\n\nChange: arm the keyboard on a tap's pointer-down and pointer-up, never on a drag, and drop it 400 ms after a tap only if nothing took focus. Covered by a host test; not yet verified on an iPhone or the Pixel.\n\nOpen: confirm on iPhone (Safari and Chrome) and Android Chrome.","files":null}]}